\ulnone\cf2  while he was still in office \u8211  now that he is calling for the current government to consider the move.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260
\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Morrison said there \u8220 just simply wasn\u8217 t the window\u8221  between the Magnitsky-style sanctions laws passing the parliament in December 2021 and the election in May 2022.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2     Scott Morrison gives a speech at a symposium of the Inter-Parliamentary Alliance on China in Tokyo. Photograph: Androniki Christodoulou/Reuters   }{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 He addressed the issue this afternoon after delivering a speech to a symposium in Tokyo organised by the Inter-Parliamentary Alliance on China, a group of parliamentarians that urges democracies to take a strong coordinated stand against the Chinese Communist party:}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 To be honest when we did all the sanctions off the invasion of Ukraine, we did it not under Magnitsky, we did it under the other [autonomous sanctions] regime that was already there because we could create a country [specific] regime. Magnitsky is great. But it\u8217 s not the whole cake. It\u8217 s a slice. And it\u8217 s an important one, because it gives you discretion, flexibility, you can move fairly quickly and that\u8217 s good.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 We could not or would not have \u8211  I don\u8217 t think ever \u8211  have moved on any sanction issue with respect to China without Magnitsky laws.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And the challenge for us was we came into our Magnitsky laws at the end of 2021, we moved through a fairly comprehensive process to consider the first round of them. That got us to mid-March. There was an election in May. And if you\u8217 re going to \u8211  particularly in the Indo-Pacific \u8211  for countries like Japan and Australia,  if you\u8217 re going to go down the path of applying sanctions in your own region in particular there\u8217 s got to be a bit of dialogue amongst partners as well. You don\u8217 t just drop this on the table. And from our government\u8217 s point of view there just simply wasn\u8217 t the window between that first round and when the election was.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But there was a lot of work done about what could be done. So that\u8217 s why it\u8217 s appropriately now the consideration of the new government and I wish them well with that.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}
