\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  Joe Martin-Jard, the CEO of the Northern Land Council in the NT, suggests that Dutton should \u8220 quietly listen\u8221  and come at the process with an \u8220 open heart\u8221 .}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 \u8220 He should come to this with an open mind and an open heart and be prepared to listen to Aboriginal people, engaging them on Country meetings and talking in quiet spaces in a quiet way and listening. That might help progress the debate,\u8221  Martin-Jard told estimates.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Thorpe interjects here, asking if Stewart\u8217 s questioning is \u8220 free advertising for the voice\u8221 , and the Labor senator Louise Pratt, chair of today\u8217 s committee, fires back that it\u8217 s not a point of order and senators can ask what questions they want of witnesses.}
